# A Russian radio interview: have you ever cooked borscht?
subtitle: "Вы когда-нибудь готовили борщ? Tom goes on the radio: have-you-ever questions, aspect in answers, and the phrases of an interview."
tags: ["russian","russian interview","russian aspect","radio","russian listening"]
teaches: ["phrases/interviews","grammar/aspect","phrases/formal-register"]
thumb: "band \"On Russian radio\" note \"Have you ever…?\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Proud and worried in Russian: гордиться, волноваться","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/157-russian-feelings-cases.cast"}

## A Russian radio interview: have you ever cooked borscht?
